Adding an icon.

* Step 1: Draw a square icon in Inkscape.

* Step 2: Export to png
Export your drawing from Inkscape as a 192 × 192 pixel PNG for
this xxxhdpi resource. Android's standard launcher icon sizes are
48, 72, 96, 144 and 192 pixels across the density buckets. 

The folder structure is:
res/
└── mipmap-xxxhdpi/
    └── ic_launcher.png

* Step 3: Update AndroidManifest.xml
Then, in AndroidManifest.xml, inside your existing <application>
element, add the android:icon attribute: 
 #+BEGIN_SRC xml
 <application
    android:label="My App"
    android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher">
 #+END_SRC

* Different densities

| Folder  | Icon size | Scale |
|---------+-----------+-------|
| mdpi    |        48 |     1 |
| hdpi    |        72 |   1.5 |
| xhdpi   |        96 |     2 |
| xxhdpi  |       144 |     3 |
| xxxhdpi |       192 | 4     |

Folder	Icon size	Density scale
mipmap-mdpi	48 × 48	1×
mipmap-hdpi	72 × 72	1.5×
mipmap-xhdpi	96 × 96	2×
mipmap-xxhdpi	144 × 144	3×
mipmap-xxxhdpi	192 × 192	4×
